type":"text","value":" could me made more precise by inferring the schema input type. In practice, this has almost 0 real world impact so it's not worth the added type complexity."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"see","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"https://github.com/TanStack/db/pull/209#issuecomment-3053001206"}]}],"headings":[{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"t","text":"T","level":3},{"id":"toperation","text":"TOperation","level":3},{"id":"remarks","text":"Remarks","level":2},{"id":"see","text":"See","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\ntype ResolveTransactionChanges<T, TOperation> = TOperation extends \"delete\" ? T : Partial<T>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/db/src/types.ts:88](https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/db/src/types.ts#L88)\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### T\n\n`T` *extends* `object` = `Record`\\<`string`, `unknown`\\>\n\n### TOperation\n\n`TOperation` *extends* [`OperationType`](OperationType.md) = [`OperationType`](OperationType.md)\n\n## Remarks\n\n`update` and `insert` are both represented as `Partial<T>`, but changes for `insert` could me made more precise by inferring the schema input type. In practice, this has almost 0 real world impact so it's not worth the added type complexity.\n\n## See\n\nhttps://github.com/TanStack/db/pull/209#issuecomment-3053001206\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: ResolveTransactionChanges\ntitle: ResolveTransactionChanges\n---\n\n```ts\ntype ResolveTransactionChanges<T, TOperation> = TOperation extends \"delete\" ? T : Partial<T>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/db/src/types.ts:88](https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/db/src/types.ts#L88)\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### T\n\n`T` *extends* `object` = `Record`\\<`string`, `unknown`\\>\n\n### TOperation\n\n`TOperation` *extends* [`OperationType`](OperationType.md) = [`OperationType`](OperationType.md)\n\n## Remarks\n\n`update` and `insert` are both represented as `Partial<T>`, but changes for `insert` could me made more precise by inferring the schema input type. In practice, this has almost 0 real world impact so it's not worth the added type complexity.\n\n## See\n\nhttps://github.com/TanStack/db/pull/209#issuecomment-3053001206\n"}
